<title>CANADA: Imasco Q4 loss after charge turns to profit.</title>
<headline>Imasco Q4 loss after charge turns to profit.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr    Profit	   C$0.70     Loss	C$0.76</p>
<p> Net    Profit	  164,000     Loss     177,000</p>
<p> Revs		   2,906,000		2,487,000</p>
<p>		MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr    Profit	   C$2.55   Profit	C$0.91</p>
<p> Net    Profit	  601,000   Profit     221,000</p>
<p> Revs		  10,736,000		9,866,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 232,051		  233,539</p>
<p>(All data above 0000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>Note: Full company name is Imasco Ltd. In December 1995, the company's Hardee's Food Systems unit recorded a special charge of C$325 million, related predominantly to the decision to sell its Roy Rogers restaurants.</p>
<p>((Reuters Montreal bureau 514-985-2434))</p>
